Experienced in analyzing oncological datasets from various sources including TCGA/GDC, Flatiron, ICGC, Tempus, MMRF, and others. Proficient in data preprocessing, model creation, and model interpretation. Strong interest in the development of statistical and machine learning models applied to medical data, with a focus on causal methods, high dimensional variable selection, and interpretability. Skilled in working with high dimensional genomic data and clinical variables. Proficient in various techniques such as logistic regression, neural networks, support vector machines, genetic algorithms, statistical signal processing, inverse problem theory, sparse coding, and simulation and modeling. Develop and maintain 4 R packages for internal use in data preprocessing, visualization, machine learning, and analysis.

